SEO OPTIMIZATION AGENT

// Project demo in Readme.md file //

Overview
This project is an automated n8n workflow that performs an end-to-end SEO audit on any target web page. It scrapes the page HTML, checks on-page SEO factors, 
generates simulated Search Console metrics, runs technical performance checks through PageSpeed Insights, gathers top competitor content from search results, uses Llama 3.3 via Groq to create optimization recommendations, 
saves the report to Airtable, and sends an email notification to request human approval before finalizing the update.

---

Node List (20 Nodes)
1. Node Name: When clicking 'Execute workflow'
Type: Trigger
Purpose: Starts the workflow manually with test inputs.
2. Node Name: Set Inputs
Type: Set
Purpose: Defines input variables such as targetUrl and targetKeyword.
3. Node Name: HTTP Request
Type: HTTP Request
Purpose: Downloads the raw HTML source code of the target page.
4. Node Name: HTML
Type: HTML
Purpose: Extracts HTML elements like title, meta description, headings, canonical link, and body text.
5. Node Name: On Code Metrics
Type: Code
Purpose: Calculates word count, keyword density, header count, and content structure metrics.
6. Node Name: Mock GSC Data
Type: Code
Purpose: Generates simulated Search Console metrics like clicks, impressions, position, and CTR based on page structure signals.
7. Node Name: Code in JavaScript
Type: Code
Purpose: Formats and structures technical data before passing it down the pipeline.
8. Node Name: PageSpeed Audit
Type: HTTP Request
Purpose: Queries the Google PageSpeed Insights API for technical performance and SEO health scores.
9. Node Name: Parse PageSpeed
Type: Code
Purpose: Extracts Core Web Vitals (LCP, CLS, FID) and specific failing audits from the PageSpeed API payload.
10. Node Name: Merge
Type: Merge
Purpose: Combines on-page metrics, simulated search data, and PageSpeed audit results into a single dataset.
11. Node Name: Competitor Research
Type: HTTP Request
Purpose: Calls the Tavily API to search and retrieve top-ranking content for the target keyword.
12. Node Name: Code in JavaScript1
Type: Code
Purpose: Prepares combined competitor and page data into a clean structure for the AI prompt.
13. Node Name: Groq Chat Model
Type: Language Model
Purpose: Provides the Llama-3.3-70B model via Groq as the AI backend for analysis.
14. Node Name: Generate SEO Plan
Type: LLM Chain
Purpose: Sends all aggregated audit data and prompt instructions to the AI model to build an optimization strategy.
15. Node Name: Parse LLM Response
Type: Code
Purpose: Cleans the AI output, verifies JSON structure, and applies fallback defaults if parsing fails.
16. Node Name: Merge1
Type: Merge
Purpose: Combines the structured AI recommendations with the original gathered data.
17. Node Name: Log to Airtable
Type: Airtable
Purpose: Writes a new audit record into Airtable containing all collected metrics and AI suggestions.
18. Node Name: Send a message
Type: Gmail
Purpose: Sends an email notification with an audit summary and an approval action link.
19. Node Name: Wait
Type: Wait
Purpose: Pauses workflow execution until the email recipient clicks the approval link.
20. Node Name: Update record
Type: Airtable
Purpose: Updates the audit record status in Airtable to Approved once approval is received.

---

Execution Steps
Step 1: The workflow starts manually and receives input parameters (target URL and target keyword).
Step 2: HTML is fetched from the URL and parsed to calculate on-page SEO metrics.
Step 3: Simulated search console performance data is generated alongside real-time PageSpeed Insights data.
Step 4: The Merge node combines all collected page and technical metrics together.
Step 5: Competitor research is gathered via Tavily API and structured alongside the page data.
Step 6: Groq Llama-3.3 processes the full dataset and creates actionable recommendations.
Step 7: AI output is formatted, validated, and merged back with the original record data.
Step 8: The workflow logs a complete record into Airtable.
Step 9: An email is sent to stakeholders, and execution pauses at the Wait node.
Step 10: Upon clicking the approval link, the workflow resumes and updates the record status in Airtable to Approved.

