Tools and APIs
* n8n: Workflow automation engine used to manage triggers, logic, and data flow.
* Google PageSpeed Insights API: Free API used for performance and technical SEO metrics.
* Tavily Search API: Web search API used to fetch high-ranking competitor content.
* Groq (Llama-3.3-70B): High-speed AI model used for data analysis and generating structured SEO plans.
* Airtable: Cloud database used to store audit records and keep track of approval statuses.
* Gmail: Email service used for human-in-the-loop approval workflows.

---

Design Details
Mock Search Console Data
The official Google Search Console API requires verified domain ownership, which limits testing on arbitrary URLs. The Mock GSC Data node generates reactive estimates based on real page signals (keyword presence, word count, density). This 
node can easily be replaced with a live Search Console API call when auditing owned domains.

Human Approval Safety Gate
To prevent automated updates or suggestions from being pushed without review, the workflow uses a Send a Message node followed by a Wait node. Execution stops until a team member manually reviews the email summary and clicks the approval link.

Separation of Extraction and Logic
Extraction and calculation tasks are divided into separate nodes (HTML, On Code Metrics, Parse PageSpeed). Keeping data extraction separate from calculation logic ensures that changes to HTML selectors or API structures do not break 
downstream data processing or LLM prompting.

